# MongoDB

> MongoDB is the world’s leading modern and multi-cloud database which uses document model and is AI ready. Founded in 2007, MongoDB document model eliminates operational complexity while ensuring unmatched resilience, scalability, and enterprise-grade security.

## How agents should use this file

> For discovering our current products, features, and capabilities and to learn about who we are.
> For implementation details (code, configuration, query syntax, APIs) use the [technical documentation index](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/llms.txt) instead.

## Key Concepts

- **Document Model**: data is stored as BSON documents (JSON-like), organized into collections inside databases. There are no rigid schemas by default.
- **MQL**: MongoDB Query Language — used for CRUD, aggregation pipelines, and vector search queries. It is NOT SQL. Documents are queried and mutated via methods like `find()`, `insertOne()`, `updateOne()`, `aggregate()`.
- **Atlas vs Self-Managed**: MongoDB Atlas is the hosted cloud service (recommended for most use cases). MongoDB Community Edition and Enterprise Advanced are self-managed options. Atlas adds managed services like Vector Search, Search, Stream Processing, and Charts.
- **Connection String Format**: `mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/<dbname>?retryWrites=true&w=majority`
- **MCP Server**: MongoDB provides an official MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that lets AI agents interact with MongoDB deployments directly in natural language.

